 true. So we can have multiple candidates with dispatch_allocated true simultaneously, each linked to the same dispatch slot (since the slot is not removed). However the slot's availability toggles: after first allocation, slot unavailable; after dispatch execution, slot becomes available again; then we allocate to second candidate, making slot unavailable again; after second dispatch, slot available again; etc. So at any time after an allocation but before dispatch, slot is unavailable; after dispatch, slot becomes available again. So to have multiple candidates with dispatch_allocated true and dispatched true, we need to allocate, dispatch, allocate, dispatch, allocate, dispatch. At the end after the last dispatch, slot will be available again (since each dispatch releases). Goal does not require dispatch_slot_available; it's not mentioned. So final state can have dispatch_slot_available true or false; not constrained.

Thus we can achieve goal by allocating dispatch slot to each candidate, then executing dispatch for each, in any order, and after each dispatch the slot becomes available again for next allocation.

Goal also requires dispatch_ready for each candidate. The action mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready set dispatch_ready for those availabilities. For schedule candidate, we need dispatch_ready shift_candidate_beta: there is no explicit action to set dispatch_ready for schedule candidate? Actually there is dispatch_ready predicate used for candidates; it is set by finalize_candidate_direct? Let's check: finalize_candidate_direct effect includes (dispatch_ready ?candidate). Also finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation and finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation also set dispatch_ready ?candidate. So after finalizing shift_candidate_beta, we will have dispatch_ready shift_candidate_beta.

For origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha, we need dispatch_ready. There are actions mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready. Their preconditions: origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready ?origin_availability. Similarly for destination.

Thus after we have transport leg assembled and loading authorized, we can mark them dispatch ready.

Goal also requires dispatched for each candidate. We'll execute dispatch after allocating slot.

Now we need to also ensure vehicle availability after dispatch: goal requires vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha and vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta. Currently vehicle_unit_alpha allocated to origin_availability_alpha, vehicle_unit_beta allocated to destination_availability_alpha. After we dispatch those availabilities, the vehicle will become available (effect of execute_*_dispatch includes vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit). So after dispatching origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha, their vehicles become available.

